 "about_text": "Hauser & Wirth Downtown Los Angeles is the Los Angeles outpost of the international gallery founded in 1992 in Zurich by Iwan Wirth, Manuela Wirth and Ursula Hauser. The Los Angeles space opened in March 2016 in the Arts District, occupying the historic former Globe Mills flour-mill complex, restored in consultation with Selldorf Architects. The campus combines exhibition galleries with an open-air courtyard, garden and the Manuela restaurant, and hosts a robust learning and community-engagement program built around partnerships with local schools, universities and nonprofits. As part of the wider Hauser & Wirth program, the Los Angeles gallery presents historically minded surveys alongside contemporary exhibitions, drawing on the gallery's roster of more than ninety living artists and artist estates spanning painting, sculpture, photography and installation across generations and geographies.",
